    "narrative": "Our primary objective today is capitalizing on favorable matchups against softer rotations to sustain our 5x5 standing. **James Wood** (76.28) and **Austin Riley** (73.19) lead the way as our strongest plays. **James Wood** benefits from an ideal matchup against Ed Rodriguez, pairing elite xwOBA metrics with a favorable 4.84 xERA, while **Austin Riley** finds himself in a high-scoring environment boosted by a massive +16% park factor. Similarly, **Brice Turang** (72.70) is locked into a prime #3 hole against Sugano, whose 5.12 xERA offers significant upside for both counting stats and AVG protection. These three anchors carry the highest efficiency ratings, and we are leaning heavily into their situational advantages to drive our daily offensive output.\n\nPlatoon edges and SB potential remain our secondary focus, especially with **Corbin Carroll** (60.09) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.68) capitalizing on their respective order placements. Despite facing a tough arm in Palmquist, **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s projected sprint speed against a slow delivery remains a core component of his high floor. Conversely, **Zach McKinstry** (43.39) was the closest candidate to cracking the lineup from the bench, but he was ultimately excluded due to his lower baseline efficiency and unfavorable platoon split against the right-handed Way. We continue to prioritize rostered players who offer dynamic speed metrics like **Jose Caballero**, though we remain cautious of the volatility in his lower-order placement against the tough southpaw Jes\u00fas Luzardo.\n\nRisks today are concentrated on our \"Lineup Pending\" designations, specifically for **Josh Naylor**, **Max Muncy**, **Cole Young**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **James Wood**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Jose Caballero**. While the optimizer assumes their historical positions, any shifts down the order will adjust our efficiency expectations downward. Furthermore, while we monitor weather, **Edwin Arroyo** was kept on the bench not just for his lower 41.76 score, but due to a 42% rain risk that further diminishes his value relative to our active starters. We will monitor official lineups closely to ensure the calculated bonuses for **Cole Young** and **James Wood** remain valid before the first pitch.",
